# Nagrek guardrails

- Next.js 16 App Router. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using a Next API. The request gate is `proxy.ts`.
- Supabase Auth, Postgres, Realtime, and Storage. Every table keeps RLS. Server actions check the caller.
- Secrets stay in `.env`. Never print them, never commit `.env.local`, never put a coupon code in client code.
- Location is approximate. Calls are not recorded by default. The age gate is 18, and the client receives age in years, not the date of birth.
- Client state stays in the session store plus sessionStorage or localStorage. Do not add Redux or Zustand.
- Do not overwrite an existing skill, rule, or agent. The frontend skills already in `.cursor/skills/` stay as they are.
- The user runs new SQL in the Supabase SQL editor. Do not apply it yourself.
- Do not commit unless the user asks.
